From e883977e2ce70709a3b22b361a4493314d73324e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PD rockets contributor <contributor@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 09:05:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep a landing's work to the frames that can move its slot

A landing followed its slot every frame: it placed the marker, then read every card's place for the move's animation, and the style it had just written forced a layout. On a board of 200 cards with a 4x slower CPU each pending frame took about 13 ms, and the drop's own task built the marker and measured the card, about 10 ms more before the first paint. Now the landing is built a frame after the drop, a tick reads everything before it writes, the scrolling ancestors are found once, and ticks run only after a change in the board, scrolling, resizing, or while an animation runs there; the move's animation is armed after such a change, when animations settle, and once a second.
